1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bat_Assad-1 Wikitree - Adoa bat Assad]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Date Estimation and Family Members===
2 CONT
2 CONT "Numerous sources make Adoa bat Assad to be the daughter of Asad ibn Hashim, and the same person as his daughter Adai binte Assad bin Hashim. This poses a dating difficulty because Asad's best estimated birth is 485, he died prior
2 CONC  to Muhammed's birth in 571, and Asad's children were likely born in the time frame 516-536. Adoa on the other hand, is said to be born in 610, and married Bustanai, born in 600. This conflict is not resolved, but in the interim, 
2 CONC Adoa has been de-linked as a daughter of Assad.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Date Estimation and Contemporary Events===
2 CONT
2 CONT If Adoa was born about 610, assume that she married at the age of 20, in 630. Her children's birth year estimation would be 631 and 633.
2 CONT
2 CONT The narrative in this profile assumes movement of peoples between Mesopotamia and Quraish, since her father was a Quraishi chieftain but her mother was the daughter of an exilarch.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 622, Muhammed, prophet of the new Islamic religion, arrived in Yathrib (now Medina) and negotiated peace between the various tribes there, including the Banu Qurayza, the Quraish Jewish tribe. In 627, believing that the Banu Qu
2 CONC rayza had betrayed an alliance, the male members of the tribe were executed and the women and children enslaved. This account is disputed by some scholars. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The narrative in this profile would assume that Adoa was not in Quraish by 627. Perhaps she was already married to Bustanai by then."
