1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Mariage d'Habibai ben Natronai David avec Rolinde d'Aquitaine Habibai ben Natronai David épouse en 730 Rolinde d'Aquitaine, fille de Norbert d'Aquitaine et Berthe de Neustrie. Leurs enfants sont : Makhir ben Habibai David ou Theod
2 CONC oric ou Teodric ou Thierry Ier d'Autun dit le Pieux (725 ou 730-793 ou 796), Comte d'Autun, qui épousera en en 744 ou 750 ou 755 Aude de France, Sigisbert ou Gilbert de Rouergue (750-820), Comte de Rouergue.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.histoireeurope.fr/RechercheLocution.php?Locutions=David
2 CONT
2 CONT Rolinde was born about 0710, the daughter of Norbert d'Aquitaine and Berthe de Neustrie. The place is not known. Her husband was Habibai ben Natronai David (comte d'Autun). They were married, but the date and place have not been f
2 CONC ound. Their two known children were NN (c0730-?) and Gilbert (?-?).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Aquitaine-175
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father was Norbert d'Aquitaine, born in Laon, Aquitaine, about 680 ref name="neal"/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Her mother was stated to be Gisela Bertrada (Unknown) Laon born Laon 722 [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriages are sometimes shown Rolinde d'Aquitaine, born 695 in Autun, and Haninai, born 700 in Babylonia. She is also sometimes shown as married to Habibai bar Aloi, born 702 or Habibai ben Natroni, born 683, both in Babylonia. Th
2 CONC ere is no documentation of such marriages, which are a part of the Space: Legend of Makhir of Narbonne in which a legendary rabbi and exilarch named Makhir who was sent from Babylon to the Frankish Court and then sent to Narbonne 
2 CONC in the region of Autun and Septimania.
2 CONT
2 CONT Neal also shows a marriage to Habibai ben Natronai David, born about 720.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was shown married to Dagobert (Merovingian) Franken, born 698 [5] She has been shown in some genealogies as the wife of Dagobert III, however, the wife of Dagobert III is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT
2 CONT She died about 720 in Toulouse, Haute-Garonne, Midi-Pyrénées, France [2][3][4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Rolinde is sometimes shown with the following children, all of whom have been dis-connected from her profile because of the problems noted below:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Gilbert Rouergue, born 750 in Rouergue. [1] Gilbert is a real person, the first known Count of Rouergue, but his parents are unknown, and his birth year is approximately 30 years later than the death of Rolinde.
2 CONT * Makhir is sometimes shown as the son of Haninai, born about 700, and Rolande d'Aquitaine, born in Autun about 695. Because the best evidence is that Makhir never actually existed, he is not linked as a child of these parents, bu
2 CONC t this link is provided in their biographies.
2 CONT * Theuderic (UNKNOWN) Merovingian IV born 711 is sometimes shown as the daughter of Rolinde and Haninai or Habibai, as part of the Space: Legend of Makhir of Narbonne because of the legendary supposition that Theuderic and Makhir 
2 CONC were the same person.
