1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The earliest translator of the “Almagest” into Arabic was the Jew Sahl al-Tabari. Another translation was made a little later (in 829), on the basis of a Syrian version, by al Hajjaj ibn Yusuf. Also called '''Rabba
2 CONC n al-Tabari''', meaning the Rabbi of Tiberias. Flourished about the beginning of the ninth century. Jewish astronomer and physician. The first translator of the Almagest into Arabic.
2 CONT
2 CONT H. Suter: Die Mathematiker und Astronomen der Araber (l0, 1900); 
2 CONT
2 CONT M. Steinschneider: Die arabische Literatur der Juden (23-34, Frankfurt, 1902). 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.usc.edu/schools/college/crcc/private/cmje/heritage/History_of_Islamic_Science.pdf
