1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Samuel ben Daniel ben Azariah was the eldest of the four sons of the Palestinian gaon Daniel ben Azariah (1051–1062). He was born around 1050, and when his father died, he moved with his mother and siblings to Dama
2 CONC scus. By 1074, Samuel was the head of the Jewish community in Damascus and of a rabbinic court there. He bore the yeshiva title “third” and also the title of nasi. Samuel was the probable author of a florid public epistle announci
2 CONC ng his father’s death, the middle part of which has survived in the Cairo Geniza.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marina Rustow
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliography
