1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Saʿadya ben Judah
2 CONT
2 CONT Saʿadya ben Judah, the scion of a family of physicians and heads of the Jewish community of Egypt, was a son of the nagid	 Judah ben Saʿadya. Since Judah died when Saʿadya was a child, the leadership of Egyptian Jewry passed to hi
2 CONC s uncle, Mevorakh ben Saʿadya, and thus Judah never became nagid or raʾīs al-yahūd (head of the Jews).  He was still active in the Jewish community when his uncle received the title nagid in 1094. The title rayyis granted to Saʿad
2 CONC ya ben Judah in a poetic dirge did not indicate an official position in the community but rather a high rank at the Fatimid court or in a government bureau. The Palestinian yeshiva titled him segan ha-yeshiva u-mesosa (chief of th
2 CONC e yeshiva and its joy).
2 CONT
2 CONT Marina Rustow
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliography
2 CONT
