1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mann (Text and Studies, I: 220 n. 43; 252-3 n. 14) convincingly argues that this Gaon is actually the one being referred to in the letters of R. Shmuel b. Eli (Assaf, p. 67). Brendan Goldman argues that the yeshiva
2 CONC  was eclipsed by the creation of the office of the Nagid by Al-Afdal in 1193, appointing Ovadiah b. Ullah as Nagid Eretz Yisrael v’Yehudah (Brendan, dissertation, pp. 272-277). The Nagid’s letter of appointment is found in T-S Ar.
