1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ṣemaḥ Ṣedeq ben Isaac served as gaon of Sura from sometime after 987 until before 999. He was the first gaon of the Sura academy after the four-decade closure that began in 942. A grandson of Ṣemaḥ ben Palṭoy, gaon
2 CONC  of Pumbedita from 872 to 890, Ṣemaḥ Ṣedeq corresponded with Elhanan ben Shemariah, whom he knew as a student of Sherira and Hay Gaon in Pumbedita, and he made efforts to strengthen ties between Sura and Fustat. In letters he wrot
2 CONC e to Elhanan preserved in the Cairo Geniza, Semaḥ explained his position on theological topics such as God's unity and attributes.  He probably also had strong connections to Qayrawan, especially if Gil is correct that Sura reopen
2 CONC ed because of the success of Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAṭāʾ, the court physician of the Zirid rulers of Ifrīqiya, in raising funds from Maghrebi merchants. Ṣemaḥ Ṣedeq was predeceased by his only son, Palṭoy, who was chief judge of the court (
2 CONC av bet din) of Sura during his father’s gaonate. He was succeeded by Samuel ben Hophni.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marina Rustow
