2 CONT ===Comments 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Francois-de-la-Mede/6000000040426023833 was not the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Rabeinu-Yitzchak-Yosef-Hanassi-Hanassi-ben-Zrachya-HaLevi/6000000212998923840
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.geni.com/discussions/304966?msg=1803296
2 CONT
2 CONT Asking Google AI: Who is behind "fringe" history that would state that a genealogical connection between a François de Méde and Yitzchak Yosef Hanassi ben Zrachya Halevi? This is the answer shown below:
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a specific niche of fringe history, often referred to as Davidic Descent research, which seeks to prove that various European noble houses (like the "de Méde" or "Medici" families) are actually descended from the Hebrew E
2 CONC xilarchs (Nesi'im).
2 CONT
2 CONT The Goal: These researchers attempt to bridge the gap between the Jewish Halevi or Ibn Yahya lines and the European aristocracy.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Method: They often cite non-existent books—such as the "La Maison de Méde" supposedly by Arthur de la Borderie—to give their claims a veneer of scholarly authority. In reality, Arthur de la Borderie was a specialist in Breton 
2 CONC history and never wrote about Sephardic-Levite genealogies.
2 CONT
2 CONT So, lets be careful to accept only bonafied, provable, documented genealogies.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
