1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bakr Ben Yahia I
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Bakr Ben Yahia I was possibly a son of Yahia Ben Yahi III and the father of Yahia Ben Bakr. He was, apparently, the first of his branch of the family to become a Christian and thus a Mozarab (Iberian Christian living under Muslim 
2 CONC domination), since his father was still and always a Jew and his son was always mentioned as being a Christian.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Bakr Ben Yahia's greatgrandson, Aloandro Ben Bekar, Governor of Faro, would see his daughter Madragana become a mistress to king Afonso III of Portugal, and ancestor of many celebrities.
