1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gersonides '''Levi ben Gershon'''] (1288 – 20 April 1344), better known by his Graecized name as '''Gersonides''', or by his Latinized name Magister Leo Hebraeus, or in Hebrew by the 
2 CONC abbreviation of first letters as '''RaLBaG''', was a medieval French Jewish philosopher, Talmudist, mathematician, physician and astronomer/astrologer. He was born at Bagnols in Languedoc, France. According to Abraham Zacuto and o
2 CONC thers, he was the son of Gerson ben Solomon Catalan.
