1 NOTE {geni:about_me} FRAT MAIMON or SOLOMON BEN MENAHEM:
2 CONT
2 CONT Provençal scholar; flourished in the second half of the fourteenth century. The name "Frat" is, according to Neubauer, abbreviated from "Frater." Frat Maimon was the author of four works, which are known only by quotations made fr
2 CONC om them by three of his disciples: (1) "'Edut le-Yisrael," probably a controversial treatise on religion; (2) "Neẓer Maṭṭa'i," on the philosophical explanations of the haggadot found in the Talmud; (3) a commentary on the poem "Ba
2 CONC tte ha-Nefesh" of Levi ben Abraham; (4) comments on Genesis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliography: Zunz, G. S. ii. 34; Steinschneider, Hebr. Bibl. xvi. 126; Geiger, Jüd. Zeit. iii. 285; Renan-Neubauer, Les Ecrivains Juifs Français, p. 753. http://www.jewishencyclopedia.com/articles/6327-frat-maimon
