1 NOTE {geni:about_me} This profile is commonly referenced among some groups of families who claim descent from David haMelech.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are many versions of these lines of descent. The principal ones are shown here:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1)Ibn Yachya (Don Yechia), Charlap – “The Book of Destiny – Toledot Charlap” – 1996 Arthur F. Menton. Drawn from fifteen family trees researched by the author. See explanations under “What the Experts Say, Articles”.  http://www.d
2 CONC avidicdynasty.org/chapter25.php http://www.davidicdynasty.org/chapter26.php
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Ibn Yachya (Don Yechia), Charlap – “Sefer Kidushei” Avraham Moshe Hamburger.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3) “Makor Niftakh LeBeit David” – 1969, Moshe Yair Weinstok.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4) Mentioned in Dayan Family Tree – “Yashir Moshe”, 1864, Moshe Dayan. http://www.davidicdynasty.org/about.php#   (see link to Dayan research).
2 CONT
2 CONT 5) Abarbanel – undated handwritten manuscript from the collection of the late Rabbi Shmuel Gorr, held by Chaim Freedman.  Reference was made to “Elef Margaliot” 1993, Meir Wunder.
