2 CONT About Shimon ben Hillel very little is known. He was the son of Hillel the Elder, and when Hillel died, Shimon took over his place as Nasi. It is assumed that Shimon did not live long after this, and was quickly succeeded by Shamm
2 CONC ai, who served as President of Sanhedrin while continuing to be  ABD. Shammai was later succeeded by Hillel the Elder son, Gamaliel I.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Preceded by Hillel the Elder
2 CONT *Sanhedrin President: 9CE to 9 (or 20)CE
2 CONT *Succeeded by Shammai - as Temporary President?
2 CONT
2 CONT Served as the second Nasi, after his father Hillel. His reign started 60 years before the destruction of the 2nd Temple.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Nesi'im
2 CONT
2 CONT The following were Nesi'im, that is to say presidents of the Sanhedrin.
2 CONT * Hillel
2 CONT * Rabban Shimon ben Hillel, about whom very little is known
2 CONT *Shammai
2 CONT * Rabban Gamaliel Hazaken (Gamaliel the Elder)
2 CONT * Rabban Shimon ben Gamliel
2 CONT * Rabban Yochanan ben Zakai
2 CONT * Rabban Gamaliel of Yavne
2 CONT * Rabbi Eleazar ben Azariah, who was Nasi for a short time after Rabban Gamliel was removed from his position
2 CONT * Rabban Shimon ben Gamliel of Yavne
2 CONT * Rabbi Judah haNasi (Judah the Nasi), known simply as "Rabbi", who compiled the Mishnah
2 CONT *<nowiki>------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
