1 NAME Ima Shalom
2 GIVN Ima Shalom
1 SEX F
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *[http://www.jewishencyclopedia.com/articles/8085-imma-shalom  Imma Shalom''']
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://jwa.org/encyclopedia/article/imma-shalom   '''Imma Shalom'''] (Mother of Peace) is identified in the Babylonian Talmud as the wife of R. Eliezer, a prominent sage who flourished circa 75 c.e., and the sister of Rabban Gaml
2 CONC iel of Yavneh, the head of the Sanhedrin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She is mentioned only a few times in rabbinic literature. After R. Eliezer defied his colleagues in the story about the oven of Aknai, his wife tried to save him from the harm she predicted would befall him. However, she failed be
2 CONC cause she erred regarding the New Moon (BT Baba Mezia 59b). Upon hearing her husband predict that a student who treated him disrespectfully would not finish out his week, she asked him if he were a prophet (BT Eruvin 63a). 
2 CONT
2 CONT When queried why her children were so physically attractive, she answered that when she and her husband engage in sexual intercourse he behaves as if “forced by a demon.” He does so, he told her, to avoid thinking about other wome
2 CONC n (BT Nedarim 20a–b). 
2 CONT
2 CONT In a hypothetical dispute about whether or not daughters, like sons, inherit from their fathers, Imma Shalom came before a judge. He awarded her a share of her father’s estate. Her brother bribed the judge who then reversed himsel
2 CONC f. Note that it is a woman who challenged the law of disenfranchisement of daughters. The judge sided with her, as did the Sadducees (Tosefta Yadaim 2:20; BT Baba Batra 115b; JT Baba Batra 8:1; 16a). Although the judge was exposed
2 CONC  as a fraud, his fair-minded decision struck a resonant chord with the rabbis. Maybe they placed this question in the mouth of a woman because they sympathized with the justice of her claim but could not bring themselves to rule i
2 CONC n the same manner (BT Shabbat 116b).
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>><nowiki>----------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:  Encyclopedia of Talmudic Sages, by Gershom Bader.  Page 195.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rabbi Eliezer was a brother-in-law to Rabban Gamaliel.  He married the Nasi's sister, the learned Ima Salim, if whom it is told that she confounded the injustice of a gentile judge with her wisdom.  But despite this relationship, 
2 CONC Rabbi Eliezer frequently was in conflict wit the Nasi and with his colleges.    
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT *[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eliezer_ben_Hurcanus Wikipedia] mentions her in passing as the wife of Eliezer ben Hurcabus
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://gill.biblecommenter.com/mark/15.htm Gill]:"This was a common name among the Jews.. we read (T. Bab. Sabbat, fol. 116. 1) of one Imme Shalom, or mother Shalom, wife of R. Eliezer, and sister to Rabban Gamaliel."
