2 CONT
2 CONT Consanguinity Index=10.76%
2 CONT
2 CONT Felipe II von Habsburg, Rey de España was born on 21 May 1527 at Valladolid, Castile, Spain. (5) He was the son of Karl V von Habsburg, Holy Roman Emperor and Isabel de Aviz, Infanta de Portugal. (4) He married, firstly, Maria de 
2 CONC Aviz, Infanta de Portugal, daughter of João III de Aviz, Rei de Portugal and Katherina von Habsburg, on 12 November 1543 at Salamanca, Spain. (5) He married, secondly, Mary I Tudor, Queen of England, daughter of Henry VIII Tudor, 
2 CONC King of England and Catarina de Aragón, Infanta de Aragón, on 25 July 1554 at Winchester Cathedral, Winchester, Hampshire, England. (5) He married, thirdly, Elizabeth de Valois, Princesse de France, daughter of Henri II, Roi de Fr
2 CONC ance and Catherine de Medici, in 1559 at Palacio del Infantado, Guadalajara, Spain.6 He married, fourthly, Anna Erzherzogin von Österreich, daughter of Maximilian II von Habsburg, Holy Roman Emperor and Maria von Habsburg, Infanta
2 CONC  de España, on 12 November 1570 at Segovia, Spain. (7), (4) 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 13 September 1598 at age 71 at El Escorial Palace, Madrid, Spain. (7) He was buried at El Escorial Palace, Madrid, Spain. (7)
2 CONT
2 CONT      Felipe II von Habsburg, Rey de España gained the title of Erzherzog von Österreich. He succeeded to the title of Rey Felipe II de España on 16 January 1544. (7) He was invested as a Knight, Order of the Garter (K.G.) on 24 Ap
2 CONC ril 1554. (7) He was deposed as King of Spain in 1558. He gained the title of Rei Felipe I de Portugal in 1580. (7) 
2 CONT
2 CONT      Philip, who was styled King of Naples and King of Jerusalem by his father, was given the title King of England. However, he hated everything about England - the climate, the food and the people. A little over a year after the
2 CONC  marriage to Mary, he left and returned to Spain. Mary saw him only once more, for a few weeks, in 1557. In 1588 as King of Spain, he organised the Spanish Armada with two objectives in mind - to re-establish Roman Catholicism in 
2 CONC his former wife's Kingdom and in Holland, and to protect Spanish trade with America. On 28th July, a Spanish Armada (fleet) of 130 vessels sailed up the Channel. The English fleet had faster ships and guns with longer range and de
2 CONC feated the Spanish.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Felipe II von Habsburg, Rey de España and Maria de Aviz, Infanta de Portugal
