1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johanan_HaSandlar   '''Johanan HaSandlar  -  יוחנן הסנדלר‎)] Johanan HaSandlar (lit. "Johanan the Shoemaker" or "Johanan the Sandalmaker", Hebrew: יוחנן הסנדלר‎; alternatively "Johanan
2 CONC  the Alexandrian") was a rabbi who lived in the second century (fourth generation of tannaim).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a great-grandson of Rabban Gamaliel the Elder; he also purportedly traced his ancestry back to King David. '''The earliest recorded ancestor of Rashi, the great medieval commentator, was a 33rd-generation descendant of Rabb
2 CONC i Yochanan.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The name "HaSandlar" may imply that Rabbi Yohanan earned his living as a shoemaker, but it could also indicate that he was a native of Alexandria, Egypt.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was one of the main students of Rabbi Akiva and a contemporary of Rabbi Shimon bar Yochai.
2 CONT
2 CONT Once, he went with several colleagues to the Valley of Rimmon to institute a leap-year. Rabbi Meir had just cited an opinion which he ascribed to Akiba, but the authenticity of which Johanan denied, adding, "I have waited on R. Ak
2 CONC iba standing [by his side as an advanced student] longer than you did sitting [as a mere hearer]." The learned company took umbrage at this derogatory remark, and murmured, "Johanan ha-Sandalar is a true Alexandrian [given to boas
2 CONC ting]." The incident, however, ended in reconciliation, and the disputants did not leave the session without kissing each other. Because he is called here "a true Alexandrian," it is assumed that he was a native of Alexandria.
2 CONT
2 CONT Once, he once exposed himself to great danger to obtain an authoritative halachic decision. During the Hadrianic persecutions, when many rabbis had been put to death for teaching Judaism, Rabbi Akiva was imprisoned and awaiting hi
2 CONC s doom at the command of Rufus. A marital question agitated the rabbis, and Johanan undertook to procure the closely guarded Akiva's advice upon it. Disguised as a peddler, he offered some goods for sale near the prison: "Who want
2 CONC s needles? Who wants hooks? How about private halitzah?" Akiba, looking out through an aperture, said in reply, "Do you have spindles? Do you have kasher (= "valid")?"
2 CONT
2 CONT At one time during the persecutions, Johanan and Eleazar ben Shammua left Palestine, intending to betake themselves to Judah ben Bathyra in Nisibis; but they did not carry out their intention. By the time they arrived at Sidon the
2 CONC y felt too homesick to proceed any farther, and returned.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on the 29th day of the Hebrew month of Tammuz (the same yahrzeit as that of Rashi), and was buried 200 meters from the tomb of Shimon bar Yochai in Meron, now located in Israel.
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>><nowiki>------------------------------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT
