2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ABRAHAM SENIOR (1 & 2), Grand Rabbi of Castile, Queen Elizabeth Advisor and Head of Finance of the Kingdom of Spain, was a Jewish banker and politician prominent in the fifteenth century. He was born and died in Segovia, Spain (14
2 CONC 12-1493). 
2 CONT
2 CONT     Simon Wiesenthal (5) mentions the ingratitude and weakness of character of Ferdinand, the Spanish king, the Jews, who have always supported him and his father. King John of Aragon, father of Ferdinand, kept a good relationship
2 CONC  with the Jews, having been cured of blindness by a Jewish doctor. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     Fernando was a poor prince, unable to approach the princess Isabella of Castile, who had strong suitors, as the kings of England and France. Who helped the prince to marry Isabel was Abraham Senior, with the support of the Spa
2 CONC nish Jewish community. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     Since the financial resources, to the strategy of being able to find the princess secretly in the rabbi's house, away from the eyes of opponents, and the rich silver gift offered to conquer it, were funded by the Jews of Spain
2 CONC . 
2 CONT
2 CONT     But instead of gratitude, after the success of marriage to Isabella of Castile, which resulted in the union of the kingdoms of Aragon and Castile, seized by an insane greed, ingratitude and unjustified hatred, King Ferdinand d
2 CONC ecided to pursue the Jewish people. 
2 CONT
2 CONT      Allied with evil leaders of the Catholic church, for the confiscation of property, arrest, kill and expel the Jews from Spain. 
2 CONT
2 CONT      When the decree of expulsion of Jews from Spain (March 31, 1492) became widely known, Rabbi Abraham Senior, along with his friend Isaac Abravanel, hastened to go to Queen Isabella, begging him to spare his people, without suc
2 CONC cess. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     On June 15, 1492, eighty years old, haggard and tired, along with his son, was baptized in Valladolid, in the presence of the King and Queen of Spain. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     Adopted the new Christian name Fernando Nunes Colonel'''''', and his son Rabbi Melamed Meier, the name of Colonel Fernando Perez, with the "godfathers" Isabella and Ferdinand of Castile. 
2 CONT
2 CONT    The surname "new Christian" the son of Abraham, Rabbi Meir Melamed, "Co-Ronel Perez" can be read in a mixture of Spanish and Hebrew, as "singing to God perish" while "Núñez Coronel" Abraham Senior, read as "No-Nizco-Ronel" mean
2 CONC s "remember to sing to God," in messages criptocrafadas outside the knowledge of the Spanish monarchs. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     From the day of his baptism, Their Highnesses left and they went to the synagogue secretly to pray with other Jews (Martin MONTESDEOCA, 1556, quoted in Eugenio Asensio, Delia Luisa López de León Fray Luis de Quevedo hum and ot
2 CONC her studies at the University Salamanca, 2005 ISBN 8478008462, pg 56. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     He died reciting the "Shema Israel", ancient prayer of faith of the Jewish people (Sefarad Paul A. Chami, said Ignacio López Calvo by Secret Crypto). 
2 CONT
2 CONT     With the perverse and relentless pursuit of inquisition of Spanish kings in cahoots with the Catholic Church to the Jews in Spain (confiscation of property, imprisonment and the death penalty at the stake), elderly, sick and e
2 CONC mbittered, Abraham Senior died the following year after his conversion and his son, in 1493. 
2 CONT
2 CONT THE SECRET SYNAGOGUE 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 2009, a secret synagogue was discovered in the house of Don Abraham Senior - Fernando Nunes Colonel, for  an Israeli distant descendant, Mrs Odeia Band (6), a tourist who visited the home of her ancestor in Segovia. This fact p
2 CONC roves that he continued to practice their religion secretly. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Don Abraham Senior - Fernando Nunes Colonel - married twice: widower of his first wife, Violante de Cabrera, later married to Maria Sanchez Del Rio Abulafia, having many descendants in the Netherlands, England, United States of No
2 CONC rth America, the Caribbean, Israel and Brazil. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The large house in Segovia, Spain, houses the "Didactic Centre de la Judería" (Jewish Educational Center), the centre of traditional Jewish studies in that city, with the initials "AS" Abraham Senior, at the entrance. 
2 CONT
2 CONT SENIOR ABRAHAM and supporting COLOMBO (4:05): 
2 CONT
2 CONT     Negotiations of Columbus and the kings of Spain for your navigation project had been broken to the point he had every intention of talking to the king of France. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     But influential conversations Colombo in Malaga, Spain, coordinated by Rabbi Abraham Senior unfavorable that changed the course of things (4). 
2 CONT
2 CONT     The famous explorer enlisted the help of the Jewish colleague Abraham Zacuto (author of astronomical and mathematical tables priceless, who accompanied Columbus on his voyages, and allowed Vasco da Gama discover the Cape of Go
2 CONC od Hope) and his friend Antonio Marchena Rabida. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     In those days, the talks took place in Malaga, between Columbus and two of the most prominent Jews in Spain: Senior Rabbi Abraham Isaac Abravanel and his friend. 
2 CONT
2 CONT    From these conversations the first effective financial support for the development of Colombo and the organization of a group of Jewish men embracing the cause of Colombo emerged in Malaga. These were: Juan Cabrero, Luis Santan
2 CONC gel, Gabriel Sanchez and Alonso Cavalry. 
2 CONT
2 CONT   The project was about to fail, but with the intervention of the converted Jew Luis Santangel (scribe of the royal house and treasurer of the Crown of Aragon, which enjoyed the full confidence of King Ferdinand). 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Luis Santangel influenced by Abraham Senior, paid for most of the money that was needed for the historical works of navigation. 
2 CONT
2 CONT    In the books of accounts Santángel Luis, preserved in the Archive of the Indies in Seville, is credited Santángel a game of 1,140,000 maravedis, which had given the bishop of Avila for the expedition of Columbus, with the perso
2 CONC nal contribution of 500,000 maravedis Colombo which funded the total project (1.64 million) of the budget. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     Negotiations loan in Malaga, coordinated by the Senior Rabbi Abraham with his friend Isaac Abravanel and Luis de Santagel came the material and personal support to Colombo because from these conversations led by Senior, the jo
2 CONC urney of discovery of the finances of the New World was formed. 
2 CONT
2 CONT      Other authors (including Salvador de Madariaga and Simon Wiesenthal) have speculated the yearnings of Jews who supported Colombo by shared dreams of finding shelter for the people of Moses chased by European cruel Inquisition
2 CONC  in the New World. 
2 CONT
2 CONT      Joseph Adler writes: "Tradition says that Columbus found in Málaga financial plan outlined there, receiving the promise and support that made Abraham Senior. 
2 CONT
2 CONT      Dr. Adler Kayserlig Meyer in his article about Christopher Columbus and the Jews, published in New York in 1894 says: 
2 CONT
2 CONT    "In Salamanca Colombo became a personal friend of Zacuto, who praised his scientific works. Malaga in he met Abraham and Isaac Abravanel Senior, who was the first to help in financing your business. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "The relationship between Colombo and the Jews 
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon Wiesenthal, said (5) work 
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 3: 
2 CONT
2 CONT "... We are on the night of August 2, 1492. Standing on the pier, embark Colombo sees the last sailors and other members of the expedition. He gave the order for everyone to be on board at 23 o'clock. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     Indeed, August 2, 1492 is a memorable day; according to the decree of the Spanish monarchs Ferdinand and Isabella, any Jew has the right to remain on Spanish soil after midnight that day. This decree reaches the expedition? Th
2 CONC ere are some Jews in Columbus ships? Is there any connection between his trip and the expulsion of the Jews? And finally, is there any relationship between their trip and the persecution of the Jews? ... "
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 4: 
2 CONT
2 CONT     "... The fact that Columbus was with all her crew on board at 23 hours, or one hour prior to the entry into force of the edict of expulsion, a part of numerous puzzles that are put in by Columbus and his voyage. Columbus knew 
2 CONC exactly an hour later, the Spanish police, the militia of the city and the relatives of the Inquisition would put the court to ascertain whether, despite the decree were still Jews in Spain ... "
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 5: 
2 CONT
2 CONT     "The link between Colombo and the Jews is not fortuitous, but desired by both parties. She surprised more than one investigator and was the subject of several studies in which we attempted to discover the reasons for this conn
2 CONC ection. Even today, if not yet fully clarified this conundrum. 
2 CONT
2 CONT      Numerous investigators have observed that the group of people who supported the plans of Columbus was composed mostly by Jews and baptized Jews (...). The truth is - and all historians are in agreement on this - the voyage of
2 CONC  Columbus would not have occurred without the help of these people (with the kings speech, material assistance, scientific contribution, and boating). 
2 CONT
2 CONT (...) But, once again, without the support of the Jews, Columbus would not have been able to accomplish your expedition. This can only be explained when studying the situation of the Jews in Spain at that time. "
2 CONT
2 CONT    Brazilian descendants of Abraham Senior / Fernando Nunes Colonel: 
2 CONT
2 CONT      In Brazil there are several descendants of the last rabbi of Castile, by his daughter Constance Colonel in traditional families of Bahia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT      The Matthew and Luis Lopes Franco, descendants of Colonel Fernando Nunes brothers were arrested for practicing Judaism for inquisitors in visitation in Bahia, having served time in prison in Lisbon, for professing religion pr
2 CONC ohibited by religious intolerance. 
2 CONT
2 CONT      Traditional family Bahia Carneiro da Rocha, originated in de Menezes and Ana Castro in Itaparica (who was married to Francisco de Abreu Costa Doria), a descendant of Colonel Constance, comes our ancestry until Rabbi Abraham S
2 CONC enior / Fernando Nunes Colonel. 
2 CONT
2 CONT      Bahia is also descended from this branch celebrated the Countess of Barral - Luisa Barros Daisy Portugal, cultured woman of great intelligence and vivacious educator Princesses of Brazil. According to some historians, it was 
2 CONC the great love of Dom Pedro II, the last emperor of Brazil, having notable influence at court, a fact that aroused jealousy of some ministers and royal advisers. 
2 CONT
2 CONT      Keeping intense correspondence with the Countess of Barral, even after her move to France until the death of her, Dom Pedro II died a year later, in Brazil, inconsolado, lamenting the loss of a great friend and confidant. 
2 CONT
2 CONT    The renowned Brazilian genealogist Professor Francisco Antonio Doria (7), who has researched the genealogy of de Menezes and Ana Castro, who also discovered the famous Brazilian singer and composer Chico Buarque (Francisco Buar
2 CONC que de Hollanda) is also a descendant, the Bahian side, the same Ana lived in Itaparica, by the daughter Ignacia, sister of our ancestor Manuel de Sá Doria. 
2 CONT
