2 CONC d AHJPE GIEJ. Feb/2002). http://www.arquivojudaicope.org.br/2012/pt/compilacoes/wiesenthal.html
2 CONT
2 CONT 6-http://melbourneblogger.blogspot.com.br/2011/02/segovias-secret-synagogue-revealed.html 7- Doria Family Genealogy, by Francisco Antonio Doria: doria.genealogias.org/CostaDoria.pdf
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT The Senior Coronel & Saraiva Family Segovia Castilla y Leon Spain, c. 1386 - See Complete Family Tree and Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Together with Isaac Abravanel, wrote the letter of objection to Isabella and Ferdinand on the expulsion of the Jews from Spain. Introduced King Ferdinand to Isabella.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Professor Haim Beinart in 'The Expulsion of the Jews from Spain' (p. 420), Don Abraham Senior was referred to, in a letter of 1487 from the Jews of Castile to the Jews of Rome and Lombardy as 'the Exilarch who is over
2 CONC  us'*. 'Exilarch' means 'Prince of the Captivity' or 'Head of the Exile'** (that is, de jure King of the Jews in exile), a title dating from the Babylonian Exile of 597-538 BC which appears to have survived in Mesopotamia until Ta
2 CONC merlane the Great sacked Baghdad in 1401. The title was hereditary in and exclusive to the House of David (see II Kings xxv. 27 and I Chronicles iii. 17 et seq.) but was elective amongst the immediate male members of that family a
2 CONC nd subject to rabbinic approval.
2 CONT
2 CONT Given the fact that the title appears never to have been accorded to (or used to describe) anyone not acknowledged by rabbinic authorities to be of Davidic descent, and that the misuse of such a title would have been most unlikely
2 CONC , it is reasonable to infer that Don Abraham was descended from one of those branches of the House of David that have been traced to Spain (see the Jewish Encyclopaedia) and that the title was accorded to him in an attempt to revi
2 CONC ve the Exilarchate after it had ceased to be recognised in Mesopotamia, as happened in Egypt in 1081. (Graham Senior-Milne)
