1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Información de los méritos y servicios de Juanes de Tolosa, Cristóbal Zaldívar,etc" (1593); '''Archivo General de Indias''', PATRONATO,80,N.5,R.1 - 50;  Imagen Núm: '''47''' / 301  ...  http://pares.mcu.es/ParesBu
2 CONC squedas/servlets/ImageServlet  ...  On this page:  '''Juan, Isabel, and Leonor are stated to be the legitimate children of Juanes de Tolosa and his legitimate wife Leonor Cortez Montezuma'''
2 CONT
2 CONT See a '''photograph of the original ''Archivo General de Indias'' statement (page 47) of patrimony and legitimacy of siblings Juan, Isabel, and Leonor''' in their respective profiles' "Media/Documents" sections.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''____________________'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Don Juanes de Tolosa and Dona Leonor Cortez Motezuma, who was a daughter of the Marquis Hernando Cortez and Dona Isabel Motezuma, a legitimate daughter of Motezuma, late Aztec ruler of New Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Therefore, she was the grand-daughter of Hernan Cortez and great-grand-daughter of Moctezuma, Emperor of the Aztecs.  Her father, Captain Juanes de Tolosa, was a prominent figure in the conquest and settlement of Nueva Galicia, Ne
2 CONC w Spain (Mexico).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''The Last Conquistador, Juan de Oñate and the settling of the far Southwest''''' by Marc Simmons '''''Mexico under Spain, Society and the Origins of Nationality''''' by Peggy K. Liss
