1 NOTE {geni:about_me} His grand-father was the Conquistador of Michoacan Province, Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:Origins of New Mexico Families by Fray Angelico Chavez. Page 3.
2 CONT
2 CONT Between 1660 and 1665 he was summoned before the Inquisition in Mexico City. Charged with murder and found guilty, he was banished from New Mexico. In exile, there is no mention of this family in New Mexico. Source:Origins of New 
2 CONC Mexico Families by Fray Angelico Chavez. Page 1.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''State Archives of Zacatecas'''  …  17th century Notary Records  ... [The transcriptions were done by Jaime Holcombe and provided to Nuestros Ranchos by Guillermo Tovar de Teresa.]  ...  http://www.nuestrosranchos.com/en/notary/
2 CONC view/record/814  ...  Record 814: '''1664-12-19'''  ...  Espinosa, Felipe Box: 2 Book: 4 Page(s): 140  ...  164.Arrendamiento de hacienda de mina. Zacatecas, '''19 de diciembre 1664'''. El adelantado '''Nicolás de Saldivar''', alc
2 CONC alde ordinario, albacea y tenedor de bienes de '''su madre María de Oñate Cortés''', y heredero, da en arrendamiento al capitán José de Monreal, vecino, los sitios y tierras de San Pedro, jurisdicción de Aguascalientes que arrendó
2 CONC  '''su hermano Juan de Saldivar'''. Por 4 años a 60 pesos anuales. fj. (140) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Simmons, Marc.  ''The Last Conquistador: Juan de Onate and the Settling of the Far Southwest'', University of Oklahoma Press, Norman, Oklahoma, 1991, page 189.  ...  “Her son, '''Don Nicolás de Zaldívar y Onate''', who evidently i
2 CONC nherited his grandfather’s treasured title of adelantado, '''noted in his will of 1679''' that the family had fallen into great poverty.”
2 CONT
