0 @N6000000003051269162@ NOTE [Wikipedia, "Natronai ben Nehemiah", retrieved 16 Dec 07]
1 CONT Natronai ben Nehemiah was Gaon of Pumbedita from 719 to 730; son-in-law of the exilarch Hasdai I. Vain of his family connections and secure in his position, he was so arrogant in his dealings with the students that many of them le
1 CONC ft the academy, returning only after his death (Letter of Sherira Gaon).
1 CONT
1 CONT Two responsa are ascribed to him, both relating to the return of Jews who had left their community to follow heretical leaders (Sha'are Zedek, iii. 7, 10). In one of these responsa Natronai decides that the followers of the pseudo
1 CONC -Messiah Serenus, should again be received into their community; in the other he decides against the reception of the children of certain heretic Jews who had renounced both the Talmudic and the Biblical Judaism. I.H. Weiss, howev
1 CONC er, ascribes these two responsa to Natronai b. Hilai. A number of responsa in the compilation Sha'are Zedek and elsewhere (comp. Mussafia, Teshubot ha-Ge'onim, Nos. 23, 52, 63, 83-87, 90, Lyck. 1864) bear the name of Natronai, but
1 CONC  it is difficult to decide whether they are the work of Na?ronai b. Nehemiah or of some other Natronai.
