0 @N6000000000437081564@ NOTE Name Suffix:<NSFX> Of Narbonne, Count Of Autun And Judiciar
0 @N6000000003086991712@ NOTE aka Thierry I de TOULOUSE; Judiarch of NARBONNE; Duke of TOULOUSE
1 CONT
1 CONT Notes from     britam.org/now149.html
1 CONT
1 CONT Aristocratic Descendants of David: Question regarding Makir Thierry David
1 CONT
1 CONT ....From what I understand, the David family of Rouen, who were the royal notaries for the province of Normandy, were originally a Jewish family descended from Makir Thierry (Theodoric) David, the son of Hannini David who was born
1 CONC  at Pembaditha in Babylon and was the Exilarch of the Babylonian Jews. According to this story, Thierry David, who was called Makir, and is known variously as Theodoric or Dietrich David, came to Narbonne in southern France during
1 CONC  the reign of Charlemagne, and that  many of his descendants settled in Normandy, all bearing the surname David.
1 CONT   ...Do you think that there is any truth to this? and, if there is any truth to this, 1) What is the evidence that  this family is descended from Thierry David? and 2) would descent from Thierry David mean that there is a literal
1 CONC  descent from King David through Jehoiachin?
1 CONT
1 CONT Answer: (a) In General:   Athol Bloomer <atholb13@hotmail.com>  has done much work on the family trees of Makir and related genealogical research.
1 CONT  Arthur J. ZUCKERMAN, ("A Jewish Princedom in Feudal France, 768 900". New York 1972) was the first researcher to seriously show the connections of King David, Makir, and some western aristocracies. I believe in Zuckerman's resear
1 CONC ch. There was a Jewish descendant of King David who settled in southern France and whose family played an important role in history and intermarried with the nobility of western Europe. ...The work of Zuckerman also dealt with the
1 CONC  Goths in southern France and indirectly helped confirm our conclusion that the Goths and related peoples were part of the Lost Ten Tribes of Israel.
1 CONT
1 CONT (b) Specific: You also asked: (2) Would descent from Thierry David mean that there is a literal  descent from King David through Jehoiachin?  Answer: If by Thierry David you mean Makir, Yes. Zuckerman's sources are reliable.
